  "ch2.lv.cvx": "Latency (ns)",
  "ch2.lv.say.log": "A logarithmic scale plots latencies spanning nearly five orders of magnitude on one chart: from L1 (1 ns) to DRAM (80 ns) is an 80× slowdown, and jumping to an NVMe SSD (70,000 ns) slows things down nearly another thousandfold.",
  "ch2.lv.say.lin": "A linear scale tells the unvarnished truth: the 70,000 ns SSD fills the entire bar, reducing even 80 ns DRAM to an almost invisible sliver at the far left.",
  "ch2.model.title": "Real Cache Simulator: Row-Major vs Column-Major Matrix Traversal",
  "ch2.model.how": "This is a real set-associative LRU cache sequentially reading a 16×16 double-precision matrix (2,048 bytes total, 8 bytes per element). Toggle “Row-major” or “Column-major”, adjust cache size, line size, and associativity, or click the button to benchmark both traversals on a large array directly in your browser.",
  "ch2.model.aria": "Left side shows cache hits (green) and misses (red) for each cell in a 16x16 matrix; right side shows cache set occupancy and miss rate",
